  "status": "Refused",
  "actual_commencement_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed widening of the dropped kerb and vehicular crossover is unacceptable in principle as it seeks to undermine a shift towards sustainable modes of transport for this car-free development. The provision of off-road parking for either staff or visiting members of the public would not promote active travel and instead promote vehicle use to access the site. This fails to comply with the objectives Policy 66 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed vehicle parking space, by virtue of its siting, would overhang the public highway (footpath) and create an obstacle to pedestrians. It would therefore cause harm to the walking and cycling environment and is contrary to the aims and objectives of Policies 60 and 61 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
